-- title:
--   Cardinality of the A-extendable m-torsion: m^{t+4g₀}
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0$ nonzero, $p$ prime and $p \nmid N_0$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of a fixed algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ of $\mathbf Q$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $N_0$, $p$ and $A$, that is, a morphism $\sigma_A$ from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to the base compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ over the base carrying a relative group law, together with bijections of $\mathrm{JZero}\,N_0$ with the sections over the generic point and of $\mathrm{JZeroC}$ over the residue field of $A$ with the sections over the reduction point; assume $\Lambda$ satisfies `IsJacobian` (the group law is commutative and the relative group scheme is abelian, the two bijections are additive, the generic one is Galois-equivariant, reduction of points agrees modulo $\ell$ when the relevant inputs hold, and every Hecke operator is realised by an endomorphism of $X$ over the base). Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data: a scheme $G$ over the base with a relative group law that is commutative, with $g\colon G\to\mathrm{base}\,p$ smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact, surjective with preconnected fibres, an additive and Galois-equivariant bijection from $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0p)$ to the sections over the generic point, Hecke operators realised by endomorphisms, multiplication by each positive $n$ flat and surjective, proper generic fibre, and a natural number $\mathrm{toricRank}$ among its fields. Then for every $m>0$ the subgroup $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ of $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0p)$ — the subgroup generated by those $x$ in $\mathrm{jZeroTorsion}\,(N_0p)\,m$ whose section $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ extends to the place $A$ along $\Lambda.\sigma_A$ — is finite of cardinality $$m^{\,\mathrm{toricRank}\;+\;4\,\mathrm{genusFF}(\kappa_A,\ \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,N_0))},$$ where $\kappa_A$ is the residue field of $A$, $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,N_0)$ is the subfield of Laurent series over $\kappa_A$ generated by $j$ and $j(q^{N_0})$, and $\mathrm{genusFF}(K,F)$ is the $K$-dimension of $H^1$ of the zero divisor of $F/K$.
--
--   This is the rank bookkeeping for the $m$-torsion of the connected Néron object at $p$ attached to $J_0(N_0p)$: the extendable $m$-torsion has order $m^{t+4g_0}$, with $t$ the toric rank of the special fibre and $2\cdot 2g_0$ accounting for the abelian part, which is an extension by two copies of the level-$N_0$ Jacobian over the residue field. It is used downstream in the analysis of inertia invariants and of the torsion subgroups carrying the mod-$\ell$ representation in the level-lowering argument.
